On Tue, 21 Sep 2004 21:04:56 -0800
Jeff Norton <jeff@arcticpc.com> wrote:

> If i disable eisa then it will boot ,
> kind of a pain to do all the time .

You don't have to do it all the time...  Once the system boots, log-in
as root, and run "config -f /bsd".  Then you can disable eisa, and it
will be written to the kernel, so you won't have to do it again.

